From: muOS R35S port
Subject: [PATCH] power: rk817_battery: fake finish compares rsoc in thousandths

rsoc is remain_cap (uAh) * 100 / fcc (mAh), i.e. percent * 1000 (the
other checks use 100 * 1000), but rk817_bat_fake_finish_mode() tested
rsoc == 100, so it never fired. The display then reached 100 % only on
the PMIC's own CHARGE_FINISH, which the R35S's analog 150 mA termination
does not reach in practice: on 2026-11-25 the counter hit FCC (rsoc
100.000 %) while dsoc stayed at 98 % for over an hour, the battery
current tapering 240 -> 68 mA with the status still "Charging" (the
same cause as 95 % after a night on 2026-11-19). Test rsoc >= 99 % (the
counter wobbles around 100 % by a few thousandths) with the BSP's own
current limit (<= 100 mA). The charger state is not required to be
CC/CV: in that taper the R35S's CHG_STS (0xEB) read 0 (charge off) while
the charger was online and 60 mA still flowed into the battery at a
constant 4.16 V, so the BSP condition could not hold either. Charger
online (ac or usb) replaces it; the finish algorithm then moves the
display to 100 % (+1 % per ~92 s). rk817_bat_update_info() also reset
finish_base on every update unless the PMIC said CHARGE_FINISH, so the
finish algorithm never saw time pass in fake finish (sec_finish=0 in the
trace): keep the base in fake finish too.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
---
--- a/drivers/power/rk817_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/rk817_battery.c
@@ -1442,8 +1442,8 @@
  */
 static bool rk817_bat_fake_finish_mode(struct rk817_battery_device *battery)
 {
-	if ((battery->rsoc == 100) &&
-	    (rk817_bat_get_charge_status(battery) == CC_OR_CV_CHRG) &&
+	if ((battery->rsoc >= 99 * 1000) &&
+	    (battery->ac_in || battery->usb_in) &&
 	    (abs(battery->current_avg) <= 100))
 		return true;
 	else
@@ -2461,7 +2461,8 @@
 		rk817_bat_get_capacity_mah(battery);
 	}
 
-	if (battery->chrg_status != CHARGE_FINISH)
+	if (battery->chrg_status != CHARGE_FINISH &&
+	    !rk817_bat_fake_finish_mode(battery))
 		battery->finish_base = get_boot_sec();
 }
 
